meta {
  name: Complete KEM key, self-hosted did:web (POST /v1/kem-key/complete)
  type: http
  seq: 172
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/kem-key/complete
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{sessionToken}}
}

body:json {
  {}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
}

docs {
  # POST /v1/kem-key/complete (self-hosted did:web)

  After uploading the updated `did.json` to your domain, ask Custos to check it. Custos fetches
  the live document through its SSRF-hardened client and promotes the staged key only if the
  document's `#atproto_kem` is exactly that key; it then caches the document and emits
  `#identity`. A Custos-hosted did:web needs no completion (`POST /v1/kem-key` published it)
  and answers 400 here.

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  { "kemKey": "did:key:zStagedKemKey", "status": "published" }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - `400` — no key staged, the document is not valid JSON, its `id` is not your DID, it does
    not publish the staged key, or the account's document is Custos-hosted
  - `401` / `403` — missing/invalid credential, or an agent-derived/app-password token
  - `404` / `502` — the did.json endpoint is missing or unreachable
}
